'''Torra's Quarters''' was [[Torra Doza]]'s room in [[Doza Tower]].<ref name="The High Tower" /> Her room was [[color]]ful and had a bunk, a desk and chair, several shelves, an armchair, and a [[holotable]] complete with all the latest [[flight simulator]]s, including ''[[Flight Simulator Squadron]]''. Torra decorated her room with posters and art on the walls. There was a large window with a motorized roller blind. The room could be locked from the outside, although Torra had figured out the pass code to enter into the interior panel to let herself out.<ref name="Secrets and Holograms">{{Resistance|Secrets and Holograms}}</ref>

{{Struct-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Torra's Quarters first appeared in "[[The High Tower]],"<ref name="The High Tower" /> the fifth episode of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]] of the ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' animated television series that premiered on [[October 28]], [[2018]].<ref name="Disney Press">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref> The room was identified as "Torra's Quarters" from its [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] entry,<ref name="DB">{{Databank|torra-s-quarters|Torra's quarters}}</ref> "Torra Doza's quarters" in the episode's accompanying episode guide,<ref name="TDQ">{{SW|url=star-wars-resistance/the-high-tower-episode-gallery|text="The High Tower" Episode Gallery}} {{C|Slide 6}}</ref> and as "Torra's room" in the episode's "Bucket's List Extra," which was posted to [[StarWars.com]] on [[October 29]], 2018.<ref name="BLE">{{SW|url=news/buckets-list-extra-the-high-tower-star-wars-resistance|text=Bucket's List Extra: 9 Fun Facts from "The High Tower" - ''Star Wars Resistance''|date=2018-10-29}}</ref>

